---
/**
 * The sky band under the hero, where the design puts an illustrated
 * Philadelphia skyline.
 *
 * The design rendered this as a flat-shaded WebGL city over a static
 * `skyline.png`. The 3D was dropped deliberately: three.js cost 504 KB — three
 * quarters of all JavaScript on the site — and ~2.5s of main-thread blocking on
 * the highest-traffic page, for decoration. The band keeps its place in the
 * layout and its sky colour, and the illustration returns as a plain image.
 *
 * `public/images/skyline.png` could not be transferred from the design project
 * (it exceeds the 256 KiB asset limit and arrived truncated). Drop the real file
 * in and un-comment the <img> below — nothing else needs to change. Until then
 * this is a colour field with no content, so it carries no img role and no alt
 * text: there is no image here to describe.
 */
---

<div class="relative h-[180px] lg:h-[260px] bg-brand-sky overflow-hidden" aria-hidden="true">
  {
    /* Restore once public/images/skyline.png exists — and give the wrapper back
    its role="img" and aria-label at the same time:
  <img
    src="/images/skyline.png"
    alt=""
    class="absolute -bottom-px left-0 w-full block pointer-events-none"
  />
  */
  }
</div>
